? Kaelen: Oakhaven requests medicine for crater survivors.
- Donate 1 Glitch Herb. => END
- Fund emergency supplies with 80 Gold. => END
- Offer sympathy, but save supplies for now. => END
Oakhaven Survivor: Medicine before speeches. We remember that.
Oakhaven Survivor: Gold is not protection, but it buys bandages before policy does.
Oakhaven Survivor: Then protection is still a promise waiting on proof.

~ _resolve_ironhold_request
# TODO: point each option at the node for its outcome
? Kaelen: Ironhold asks for repair stock to keep local systems independent.
- Donate 1 Data Ore. => END
- Fund clockwork repairs with 100 Gold. => END
- Decline the request. => END
Ironhold Delegate: Material support is a clearer argument than any speech.
Ironhold Delegate: Funded repairs buy us time to debate without panic.
Ironhold Delegate: Then structure will have to survive on caution alone.

~ _resolve_mirror_request
# TODO: point each option at the node for its outcome
? Kaelen: Mirror City asks for stable witness media before the crisis distorts testimony.
- Donate 1 Memory Shard. => END
- Record a public testimony instead. => END
- Leave the mirrors uncalibrated. => END
Mirror Witness: The shard holds testimony without making it obey.
Kaelen: Record this: the Source Key is not a right to be believed.
Mirror Witness: Accepted. Accountability can begin before the perfect archive exists.
Mirror Witness: Uncalibrated mirrors still reflect. They just hurt more people.

~ _oakhaven_faction
Oakhaven Survivor: We want walls. Patrols. A promise that freedom does not mean being left alone with the next crater.
Oakhaven Survivor: When the first warning came, you gave us time to move children, medicine, and stubborn elders. That time is why some of us stand here.
Oakhaven Survivor: When you left quietly, we learned the crater was spreading from the screams. Freedom cannot rely on heroes forgetting to warn people.
Oakhaven Survivor: Oakhaven's first warning record is missing. Missing warnings are how disasters become traditions.
Oakhaven Survivor: You preserved the deleted. You understand safety can be mercy, even when it feels like restraint.
Oakhaven Survivor: You released the deleted. Some of us fear you will open every gate before anyone has shelter.
Oakhaven Survivor: You bargained once. If protection has terms again, who reads the fine print for us?
Oakhaven Survivor: We do not know what kind of mercy you believe in.
Kaelen: Protection cannot become the first new cage.

~ _ironhold_faction
Ironhold Delegate: We want structure. Not tyranny. Not market chaos. Something strong enough to survive disagreement.
Seraphina: Ironhold will stand with the saved, but not under another command structure that cannot be questioned.
Seraphina Relay: Seraphina stayed behind to keep Ironhold from eating itself. She sends support, conditions, and a very pointed warning about heroes with keys.
Ironhold Delegate: You rejected Seraphina's help. Ironhold remembers. Cooperation now will need proof, not speeches.
Ironhold Delegate: Seraphina's status is unclear. Ironhold distrusts unclear chains of command.
Ironhold Delegate: You told Seraphina the truth about Root Access. Honest power is still dangerous, but at least it can be audited.
Ironhold Delegate: You were cautious with Seraphina. The city respects caution; it fears secrecy.
Ironhold Delegate: You showed off Root Access like a weapon. The assembly needs to know you have learned humility since then.
Ironhold Delegate: The first Root Access explanation never reached our records.
Ironhold Delegate: If every backup remains public, structure is the only thing between truth and panic.
Ironhold Delegate: You collapsed unstable backups. Good. A free city still needs someone willing to make hard cuts.
Ironhold Delegate: You merged selected histories. Then build laws that admit history is complicated.
Ironhold Delegate: We cannot govern around mysteries forever.
Kaelen: Structure should help people argue without needing a ruler to end the argument.

~ _mirror_faction
Mirror Witness: We demand accountability. Not speeches. Witnesses. Records. A way to challenge the person holding the key.
Mirror Witness: You rejected obedience. Then do not ask the saved to obey you because you are tired.
Mirror Witness: You rejected the perfect rescue. Then let imperfect people help make imperfect decisions.
Mirror Witness: You rejected abandonment. Then stay answerable after the cheering stops.
Mirror Witness: Your reflection never named its fear. We will name ours: unchecked heroes.
Kaelen: A revolt that cannot question me is just SOVEREIGN with applause.

~ _choir_faction
Cathedral Remnant: The Choir is silent. Its absence speaks for every dangerous system the saved want destroyed before it can repent.
Kaelen: Silence can protect people. It can also teach them that deletion is the only tool.
Cathedral Witness: The Choir remains as warning. We ask for purpose without command authority.
Kaelen: Warnings need a place in the new world, but not a throne.
Rewritten Administrator: We serve by consent now. We request a task: help the saved build systems that can be refused.
Kaelen: Then service means accepting no as a valid answer.
Cathedral Static: The Cathedral outcome is unclear. The assembly fears what it cannot classify.
Kaelen: Then we make uncertainty visible instead of letting it rule from the dark.

~ _backup_faction
Backup Historian: We are painful histories, and we remain. Recognition is not optional. We are not footnotes.
Vanished Backup Echo: Some of us are gone. The living are safer. Do not call that cost imaginary.
Merged Citizen: I remember a life I did not live. It hurts. It also helps me recognize SOVEREIGN's lies faster.
Backup Static: The backups cannot tell what became of them. Recognition begins with admitting the record is broken.
Kaelen: The new world has to make room for people who remember differently.
